# Ubuntu White Periodicity / Negamane

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    F[Managed Physical Copy] --> A[Alteration Chain]
    A --> D1[Depth 1-8: Holistic Periodicity]
    A --> D2[Depth 9-24: Epoch Periodicity]
    D1 --> H[Holistic Checkpoint]
    D2 --> E[Epoch Summary]
    H --> AR[Archive Tier]
    E --> AR
    M[Monitor Binary] --> N[Negamane Integrity Anchor]
    N --> V[Verify Binary + Config + Policy]
    V --> A
```

```mermaid
classDiagram
    class PeriodPolicy {
      policy_id
      relative_period
      epoch_length
      retention_target
      version
    }
    class Checkpoint {
      depth_band
      timestamp
      first_record
      last_record
      policy_id
    }
    class Epoch {
      number
      start
      end
      first_record
      last_record
      policy_id
    }
    PeriodPolicy --> Checkpoint
    PeriodPolicy --> Epoch
```

Negamane protects the monitor's executable, configuration, schema, and policy inputs through independently verifiable integrity controls. It does not make modification physically impossible.
